--- body ---
## Context

`data/reference/vietnam_thermal_v1.csv` is frozen at commit `85a0e6c7` for
Exp1–3 (see `data/reference/PROVENANCE.md`). The Exp2 FP audit
(`docs/fp-audit-exp2.md`) surfaced two internal-consistency problems that
directly cause FPs and mis-scoring:

**A. 17 cleaned-name collisions** (`PowerPlantDataframeCleaner.clean_name`
maps two reference rows to the same string). Two kinds:
- *True duplicates to delete*: `Dong Nai Formosa` ×2,
  `Ha Tinh Formosa Plastics Steel Complex` ×2, `Duyên Hải 2` (appears as both
  `Duyen Hai 2` and `Duyên Hải 2`).
- *Distinct plants wrongly collapsed by the cleaner*: `Cà Mau I` (gas turbine)
  vs `LNG Cà Mau 1`; `Quang Ninh 1` (coal) vs `LNG Quảng Ninh 1 (Cẩm Phả)`;
  `NĐ Ô Môn I` vs `TBKHH Ô Môn I`; `LNG Bà Rịa 2` vs `TBKHH Bà Rịa 2`;
  `LNG Long An I` vs `Long An 1`; etc. Here the `^lng` drop + roman→arabic
  substitution is too aggressive and merges a plant with its LNG successor.

**B. Mixed romanization.** 54 names are ASCII-only (`Duyen Hai 1`,
`Cam Pha 3`), 109 carry diacritics (`Duyên Hải 2`, `Phả Lại 1`). Models emit
diacritic Vietnamese, so the 54 ASCII rows are systematically harder to match —
a hidden bias in coverage/precision across all of Exp1–3.

## Why needs-human

This edits the frozen scientific reference. It requires a **new version tag**
(`vietnam_thermal_v2.csv`), a `PROVENANCE.md` entry, and a decision on whether
to re-score (cheap: re-run scoring on existing model outputs) — the model runs
themselves do not change. The collision resolutions (especially gas-vs-LNG)
need a domain call. Do not edit in place.

## Approach
1. Produce a collision report: extend `experiments/scripts/fp_audit_exp2.py`
   logic (the `seen` map) into a small checked artifact listing all 17 groups
   with row attributes, for human adjudication.
2. Delete confirmed true duplicates.
3. For distinct-but-collapsed pairs, decide the fix: either keep both with names
   that survive cleaning (e.g. retain the `LNG` token for the successor), or
   gate the `^lng` drop / roman-numeral substitution in the cleaner so a gas
   plant and its LNG project stay distinct (coordinate with 0392/0393).
4. Normalize romanization to one scheme — recommend: keep diacritic Vietnamese
   as the canonical `name`, add a romanized `name_ascii` alias column for
   robustness. Update loaders/PROVENANCE.
5. Write `vietnam_thermal_v2.csv`; bump `PROVENANCE.md`; re-score Exp1–3 from
   existing outputs and confirm no metric collapses unexpectedly.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Collision report artifact committed; 17 groups each adjudicated
- [ ] Zero `clean_name` collisions among *distinct* plants in v2
      (true duplicates removed; legitimate distinct pairs kept separable)
- [ ] Single romanization policy applied; `name_ascii` alias present
- [ ] `vietnam_thermal_v2.csv` + `PROVENANCE.md` version entry committed
- [ ] Exp1–3 re-scored from existing outputs; metric deltas explained
- [ ] `make check` passes

## First failing test
A new `tests/test_reference_integrity.py` (red→green): assert that no two rows
of the reference share a `clean_name`, and that every `name` matches the chosen
romanization policy.

## Out of scope
- Adding new plants (→ 0395, which should build on v2 here).
- Cleaner prefix/extension changes (→ 0392) and LP-veto (→ 0393), except where
  the gas-vs-LNG collision fix requires a coordinated cleaner gate.

